Canceling PLINQ queries
We can cancel a PLINQ query using the CancellationTokenSource and
CancellationToken classes. The cancellation token is passed to the PLINQ query using
the WithCancellation clause and then we can call CancellationToken.Cancel to
cancel the query operation. When a query is canceled, it throws
OperationCancelledException.
This is done as follows:
